        <h1>About</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="post-body">
        <p>Prasad Ajinkya is a software architect and engineering leader based in Mumbai, India. He serves as Head of Technology across <a href="https://homevillegroup.com">Homeville Group</a> and Bharat Housing Network, overseeing core digital infrastructure for housing finance, co-lending platforms, and automated credit systems.</p>

        <p>His work centers on the mechanical realities of Indian financial technology: developing high-throughput ingestion and underwriting engines that convert unstructured data—from multi-account bank statements and Goods and Services Tax (GST) returns to vernacular property titles—into deterministic, auditable decisions.</p>

        <p>In artificial intelligence, he favors deterministic systems over probabilistic guesswork. He is the architect of Manthan, an internal Git-backed shared memory and distributed telemetry hub that equips autonomous agents with persistent operational context, architectural invariants, and OpenTelemetry-compliant session tracing. Working alongside Dnyankosh—an institutional Model Context Protocol gateway that grounds machine tasks in statutory and architectural standards—his systems coordinate multi-agent engineering workflows across diverse foundation models in production.</p>

        <p>Since 2008, he has published <em>The Big Fat Geek</em>, documenting empirical telemetry from production AI workloads, distributed software design, and engineering management.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions, discussions, or inquiries may be directed to <a href="mailto:kidakaka@gmail.com">kidakaka@gmail.com</a>. He can also be found on <a href="https://x.com/kidakaka">X (formerly Twitter)</a>.</p>
      </div>
